<title>BRAZIL: Brazil oilworkers reject pay deal, seek more talks.</title>
<headline>Brazil oilworkers reject pay deal, seek more talks.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian oilworkers have voted to reject a pay offer from state energy monopoly Petrobras and to carry on negotiating a better deal, a union spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Results from half of ballots held by union assemblies across Brazil on Tuesday and Wednesday show that there is a &quot;clear tendency&quot; among oilworkers to reject Petrobras' offer and to remain ready for a possible strike, she said.</p>
</text>
